\title{A limit order checked to rest rather than trade before it is sent}
\description{
Indian exchanges have no post-only flag, so this can only check the book before sending; the book can still move while the order is in flight. When the order would cross, \code{on_crossing} decides: \code{refuse} answers HTTP 409 and sends nothing, and \code{rest} moves the price back to your own side's best price. A buy counts as passive anywhere below the best offer and a sell anywhere above the best bid, so a price inside the spread is sent as it is. UBI refuses a \code{market} template with \code{post_only_crosses} and a stop with \code{post_only_needs_limit}, both with HTTP 400, and with no readable book on arrival it answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and checks the book on the first tick that has one.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
